[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [[:db/retract 17592186158690 :answer-field/choices 17592186158691] [:db/retract 17592186158690 :answer-field/choices 17592186158692] [:db/retract 17592186158690 :answer-field/choices 17592186158693] [:db/retract 17592186158690 :answer-field/choices 17592186158694] [:db/retract 17592186158690 :answer-field/choices 17592186158695] {:db/id 17592186162046 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7be864d2-62c5-5172-87fe-bf187923ab8c" "question-09cc9808-be42-54c9-b4a2-69b0d9a20cf1" "question-8460a557-83b6-5efd-a8a5-c94e63881b6d" "question-37fc4f1c-699a-5034-b164-6cf41c6e46b4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161846 :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n![](images/50/501074b2c8aa951c9236dc628de2a564f31b21b5ac5b4dd34d7b1324d4c8a331.svg)\nIf $Y =1-3X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y = u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for $F_Y$ terms of $F_X,$ where $F_Y$ and $F_X$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate $F_Y$ to get the probability density function $f_Y.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y = 1-3X$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X.$  Moreover, for $0 < x < 1,$ we have $-2 \\lt y \\lt 1 .$\n\n![](images/3b/3bb641b1920d0ded33e4ffa25f3e0af856550dd3820edf30416bd79c3a6da264.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $-2 \\lt y \\lt 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(1-3X\\le y) \\\\  & =P(-3X\\le y-1) \\\\  & =P(X\\ge \\frac{1-y}{3}) \\\\  & =1-{F}_{X}(\\frac{1-y}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF $f_Y(y)$ for $-2 \\lt y \\lt 1,$ we differentiate $F_Y$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0-(-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(\\frac{1-y}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{1-y}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of $f_X,$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{1-y}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 2\\cdot (\\frac{1-y}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(1-y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n![](images/b0/b00d02901c82c0544e8e576577832184919da2338cf05d2d8a3fa230d45993c4.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162047 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-670a140c-55d4-5114-b612-9d3a283512c3" "question-f3a2a8f5-8f7b-5578-9df3-f4e28dce2d10" "question-1f799a56-7472-58ef-998d-84e22fb88853" "question-a4b19843-0372-523c-be3f-e38cf328fccc" "question-75b7b0a4-c7ee-525c-b9ca-1a7df7652ed9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161847 :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n![](images/33/3357fbadc12363114c7274b17df9f8e992566d53f8233841783338687b88989e.svg)\nIf $Y = (2-X)^3,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y = u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for $F_Y$ terms of $F_X,$ where $F_Y$ and $F_X$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate $F_Y$ to get the probability density function $f_Y.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y = (2-X)^3$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $0 \\lt x \\lt 2,$ we have $0 \\lt y \\lt 8 .$\n\n![](images/2c/2c07ffe5af282ba1689cb6f49201b979afb4186d0128dd6a97f446b7240d76d6.png)\n\n \n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $0 \\lt y \\lt 8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P((2-X)^{3}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(2-X\\le {y}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =P(-X\\le {y}^{1/3}-2) \\\\  & =P(X\\ge 2-{y}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =1-{F}_{X}(2-{y}^{1/3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF $f_Y(y)$ for $0 \\lt y \\lt 8,$ we differentiate $F_Y$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0-(-\\frac{1}{3{y}^{2/3}})\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(2-{y}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{y}^{2/3}}\\cdot {f}_{X}(2-{y}^{1/3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of $f_X,$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{3{y}^{2/3}}\\cdot {f}_{X}(2-{y}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{y}^{2/3}}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}(2-(2-{y}^{1/3}))^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{y}^{2/3}}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}(2-2+{y}^{1/3})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{y}^{2/3}}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}({y}^{1/3})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n![](images/d8/d858994c802b37d5867c0b8940848fec484bf42c48ecb525c5d518165ade60c6.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162248 :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{-4x},\\, & x>0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=2X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=2X$ is a strictly increasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $x>0,$ we have $y>0.$\n\n![](images/8b/8b2d1487d180db1df306cd8c83088ef0334d29769bd7ef94eed7f75d4e6cedf7.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $y>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(2X\\le y) \\\\  & =P(X\\le \\frac{y}{2}) \\\\  & ={F}_{X}(\\frac{y}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $y>0,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(\\frac{y}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{y}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{y}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4{e}^{-4\\cdot y/2} \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2y}, & \\,y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186158690 :answer-field/correct "answer-69593d18-dc90-550d-8f2b-fef2e3f9c883" :answer-field/choices ["answer-69593d18-dc90-550d-8f2b-fef2e3f9c883" "answer-600d0ed3-d6f7-5bed-9243-c5cd652cb251" "answer-bf7be294-62d9-5518-9eb0-0262367daae6" "answer-39e8db46-65a2-5088-a0fc-7d008a801433" "answer-0d7fa984-dcc6-51d3-a178-09d0e7e701a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69593d18-dc90-550d-8f2b-fef2e3f9c883" :answer/id #uuid "69593d18-dc90-550d-8f2b-fef2e3f9c883" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2y}, & \\,y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-600d0ed3-d6f7-5bed-9243-c5cd652cb251" :answer/id #uuid "600d0ed3-d6f7-5bed-9243-c5cd652cb251" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-4y}, & \\,y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf7be294-62d9-5518-9eb0-0262367daae6" :answer/id #uuid "bf7be294-62d9-5518-9eb0-0262367daae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}8{e}^{-8y}, & \\,y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39e8db46-65a2-5088-a0fc-7d008a801433" :answer/id #uuid "39e8db46-65a2-5088-a0fc-7d008a801433" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-4y}, & \\,y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d7fa984-dcc6-51d3-a178-09d0e7e701a1" :answer/id #uuid "0d7fa984-dcc6-51d3-a178-09d0e7e701a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-4y}, & \\,y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7be864d2-62c5-5172-87fe-bf187923ab8c" :question/id #uuid "7be864d2-62c5-5172-87fe-bf187923ab8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-151981" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}(1-{x}^{2}),\\, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=\\frac{X}{3},$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ in terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=\\frac{X}{3}$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $0<x<1,$ we have $0<y<\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\n![](images/42/42a3c2510927b66842ec0360eabfb169a306ccaf52292132f31769036e608e69.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $0<y<\\frac{1}{3},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(\\frac{X}{3}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 3y) \\\\  & ={F}_{X}(3y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $0<y<\\frac{1}{3},$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(3y) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {f}_{X}(3y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =3\\cdot {f}_{X}(3y) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(1-(3y)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}(1-9{y}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{2}(1-9{y}^{2}), & \\,0<y<\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-85d2285e-2456-56af-a314-257530350a9e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-85d2285e-2456-56af-a314-257530350a9e" :answer-field/id #uuid "85d2285e-2456-56af-a314-257530350a9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-09920ab5-927e-5144-b904-cafb0b14ca5b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b55a125e-dbc5-56ad-bd31-db73ae35ac74" "answer-2d7990c6-c565-5878-9b66-56ed047222ca" "answer-202d7c13-d634-5a77-af5c-845389655864" "answer-a839825b-9be8-5988-b3e5-e0aa662c915b" "answer-09920ab5-927e-5144-b904-cafb0b14ca5b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b55a125e-dbc5-56ad-bd31-db73ae35ac74" :answer/id #uuid "b55a125e-dbc5-56ad-bd31-db73ae35ac74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{18}(9-{y}^{2}), & \\,0<y<3 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2d7990c6-c565-5878-9b66-56ed047222ca" :answer/id #uuid "2d7990c6-c565-5878-9b66-56ed047222ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}(1-9{y}^{2}), & \\,0<y<\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-202d7c13-d634-5a77-af5c-845389655864" :answer/id #uuid "202d7c13-d634-5a77-af5c-845389655864" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}(9-{y}^{2}), & \\,0<y<3 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a839825b-9be8-5988-b3e5-e0aa662c915b" :answer/id #uuid "a839825b-9be8-5988-b3e5-e0aa662c915b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{27}{8}(1-3{y}^{2}), & \\,0<y<\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09920ab5-927e-5144-b904-cafb0b14ca5b" :answer/id #uuid "09920ab5-927e-5144-b904-cafb0b14ca5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{2}(1-9{y}^{2}), & \\,0<y<\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-09cc9808-be42-54c9-b4a2-69b0d9a20cf1" :question/id #uuid "09cc9808-be42-54c9-b4a2-69b0d9a20cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-110111" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x,\\, & -1<x<0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=10X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=10X$ is a strictly increasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $-1<x<0,$ we have $-10<y<0.$\n\n![](images/4b/4b03f4d44db5b0db0498469f80fa25e56177a8602c657d8506105837212bf5ba.png)\n\n*Note: Image not drawn to scale.*\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $-10<y<0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(10X\\le y) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 0.1y) \\\\  & ={F}_{X}(0.1y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $-10<y<0,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0.1\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(0.1y) \\\\  & =0.1\\cdot {f}_{X}(0.1y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =0.1\\cdot {f}_{X}(0.1y) \\\\  & =0.1\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0.1y \\\\  & =-0.02y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-0.02y, & -10<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a19812d1-1d0a-5303-9a54-a3aaf278c49f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a19812d1-1d0a-5303-9a54-a3aaf278c49f" :answer-field/id #uuid "a19812d1-1d0a-5303-9a54-a3aaf278c49f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f894221d-2427-5570-8811-51ea50f7082e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f894221d-2427-5570-8811-51ea50f7082e" "answer-580d8eab-cee9-52ff-8594-cc7c4cf9f774" "answer-f445b8e1-6995-53c8-b3fe-7a9a2f3140f8" "answer-533ff78c-a4d2-572e-aa52-f826f311b683" "answer-ed5095e2-f6a2-5b2f-833a-1ffb143c4f3f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f894221d-2427-5570-8811-51ea50f7082e" :answer/id #uuid "f894221d-2427-5570-8811-51ea50f7082e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-0.02y, & -10<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-580d8eab-cee9-52ff-8594-cc7c4cf9f774" :answer/id #uuid "580d8eab-cee9-52ff-8594-cc7c4cf9f774" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-200y, & -0.1<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f445b8e1-6995-53c8-b3fe-7a9a2f3140f8" :answer/id #uuid "f445b8e1-6995-53c8-b3fe-7a9a2f3140f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.002{y}^{2}, & -10<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-533ff78c-a4d2-572e-aa52-f826f311b683" :answer/id #uuid "533ff78c-a4d2-572e-aa52-f826f311b683" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.02y, & 0<y<10 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed5095e2-f6a2-5b2f-833a-1ffb143c4f3f" :answer/id #uuid "ed5095e2-f6a2-5b2f-833a-1ffb143c4f3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2y, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8460a557-83b6-5efd-a8a5-c94e63881b6d" :question/id #uuid "8460a557-83b6-5efd-a8a5-c94e63881b6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-151985" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{3},\\, & 1<x<2 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=2X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ in terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=2X$ is a strictly increasing function of $X.$  Moreover, for $1<x<2,$ we have $2<y<4.$\n\n![](images/60/60342277a025cb26cebab2ac534fad4aa1b49fc2285571c303c4e829eb464606.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $2<y<4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(2X\\le y) \\\\  & =P(X\\le \\frac{y}{2}) \\\\  & ={F}_{X}(\\frac{y}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $2<y<4,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(\\frac{y}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{y}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{y}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2(\\frac{y}{2})}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{6}, & \\,2<y<4 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-69f2e9ff-fa41-50ab-a63c-2d1d1f490067"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-69f2e9ff-fa41-50ab-a63c-2d1d1f490067" :answer-field/id #uuid "69f2e9ff-fa41-50ab-a63c-2d1d1f490067" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b5dc456d-f743-5286-851a-c035feeffac9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-165a73fa-f469-5a44-86ef-009948eb5611" "answer-0b7bf6b1-d530-59ea-9dc8-7b99db3d0094" "answer-d167a7a8-34d5-59c3-b949-f001717e3bd9" "answer-1fc1534a-6a01-51a4-9c6e-4184dd7e0bcc" "answer-b5dc456d-f743-5286-851a-c035feeffac9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-165a73fa-f469-5a44-86ef-009948eb5611" :answer/id #uuid "165a73fa-f469-5a44-86ef-009948eb5611" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}, & \\,1<y<2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b7bf6b1-d530-59ea-9dc8-7b99db3d0094" :answer/id #uuid "0b7bf6b1-d530-59ea-9dc8-7b99db3d0094" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4y}{3}, & \\,2<y<4 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d167a7a8-34d5-59c3-b949-f001717e3bd9" :answer/id #uuid "d167a7a8-34d5-59c3-b949-f001717e3bd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{3}, & \\,2<y<4 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fc1534a-6a01-51a4-9c6e-4184dd7e0bcc" :answer/id #uuid "1fc1534a-6a01-51a4-9c6e-4184dd7e0bcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{6}, & \\,1<y<2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5dc456d-f743-5286-851a-c035feeffac9" :answer/id #uuid "b5dc456d-f743-5286-851a-c035feeffac9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{6}, & \\,2<y<4 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-37fc4f1c-699a-5034-b164-6cf41c6e46b4" :question/id #uuid "37fc4f1c-699a-5034-b164-6cf41c6e46b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-110106" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2},\\, & 0<x<3 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=1-\\frac{1}{3}X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=1-\\frac{1}{3}X$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X.$  Moreover, for $0<x<3,$ we have $0<y<1.$\n\n![](images/af/afe10720ce51bc3dd1b304ea276568d0e505f90159359f5ae54462e4caa729e7.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $0<y<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(1-\\frac{X}{3}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(-X\\le 3y-3) \\\\  & =P(X\\ge 3-3y) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 3-3y) \\\\  & =1-{F}_{X}(3-3y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $0<y<1,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0-(-3)\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(3-3y) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {f}_{X}(3-3y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =3\\cdot {f}_{X}(3-3y) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}(3-3y)^{2} \\\\  & =3{(1-y)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{(1-y)}^{2},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5108732e-f4b1-55bf-ab3d-9aaa670d4ed1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5108732e-f4b1-55bf-ab3d-9aaa670d4ed1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5108732e-f4b1-55bf-ab3d-9aaa670d4ed1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8a45c7a0-ff71-52fb-9d02-51c4c15a7b53" :answer-field/choices ["answer-472e5251-de8e-5c8f-906b-4486590c0f4f" "answer-46564b22-49a3-5dd7-851e-0ef24aa530e9" "answer-8a45c7a0-ff71-52fb-9d02-51c4c15a7b53" "answer-6f344b2d-2e68-5f7d-a74f-c89cb5cf5253" "answer-53f81be5-441e-51b6-84d8-52f835d28bfb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-472e5251-de8e-5c8f-906b-4486590c0f4f" :answer/id #uuid "472e5251-de8e-5c8f-906b-4486590c0f4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2(1-y),\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46564b22-49a3-5dd7-851e-0ef24aa530e9" :answer/id #uuid "46564b22-49a3-5dd7-851e-0ef24aa530e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{(1+y)}^{2},\\, & -1<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a45c7a0-ff71-52fb-9d02-51c4c15a7b53" :answer/id #uuid "8a45c7a0-ff71-52fb-9d02-51c4c15a7b53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{(1-y)}^{2},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f344b2d-2e68-5f7d-a74f-c89cb5cf5253" :answer/id #uuid "6f344b2d-2e68-5f7d-a74f-c89cb5cf5253" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2},\\, & -1<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53f81be5-441e-51b6-84d8-52f835d28bfb" :answer/id #uuid "53f81be5-441e-51b6-84d8-52f835d28bfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-670a140c-55d4-5114-b612-9d3a283512c3" :question/id #uuid "670a140c-55d4-5114-b612-9d3a283512c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-110124" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x,\\, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y={X}^{4},$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note  that since the possible values of $X$ are $0<x<1,$ $Y={X}^{4}$ is a strictly increasing function of $X$ when $0<x<1.$ Moreover, for $0<x<1,$ we have $0<y<1.$\n\n![](images/9a/9a6f01a3538711e45e581038af5eaf95e229bf72d08bafefbcf34786a40c1d2d.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $0<y<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P({X}^{4}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(X\\le {y}^{1/4}) \\\\  & ={F}_{X}({y}^{1/4})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $0<y<1,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{y}^{3/4}}\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}({y}^{1/4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{y}^{3/4}}\\cdot {f}_{X}({y}^{1/4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{4{y}^{3/4}}\\cdot {f}_{X}({y}^{1/4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{y}^{3/4}}\\cdot 2({y}^{1/4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-38e37aa3-43fc-561c-9a91-d1b0e6848656"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-38e37aa3-43fc-561c-9a91-d1b0e6848656" :answer-field/id #uuid "38e37aa3-43fc-561c-9a91-d1b0e6848656" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ee1549c6-a005-585d-aaa9-47cb105e6439" :answer-field/choices ["answer-513b7cbf-3854-54d3-8df7-b61ae060993c" "answer-ee1549c6-a005-585d-aaa9-47cb105e6439" "answer-e1de8cd4-39ab-557a-bd23-6dbdab09b64c" "answer-100bdc8b-84b9-522b-95a8-62a7c19d7ac1" "answer-1da9150a-4f27-53df-84d6-afffbc13c04b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-513b7cbf-3854-54d3-8df7-b61ae060993c" :answer/id #uuid "513b7cbf-3854-54d3-8df7-b61ae060993c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee1549c6-a005-585d-aaa9-47cb105e6439" :answer/id #uuid "ee1549c6-a005-585d-aaa9-47cb105e6439" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1de8cd4-39ab-557a-bd23-6dbdab09b64c" :answer/id #uuid "e1de8cd4-39ab-557a-bd23-6dbdab09b64c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{y},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-100bdc8b-84b9-522b-95a8-62a7c19d7ac1" :answer/id #uuid "100bdc8b-84b9-522b-95a8-62a7c19d7ac1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4\\sqrt[4]{y}},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1da9150a-4f27-53df-84d6-afffbc13c04b" :answer/id #uuid "1da9150a-4f27-53df-84d6-afffbc13c04b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt{{y}^{3}},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f3a2a8f5-8f7b-5578-9df3-f4e28dce2d10" :question/id #uuid "f3a2a8f5-8f7b-5578-9df3-f4e28dce2d10" :question/math-academy-id "q-110130" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\, & x>1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=\\frac{1}{X},$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that the possible values of $X$ are $x\\in (1,\\infty ),$ and $Y=\\frac{1}{X}$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X$ when $X>1.$\n Moreover, for $x>1,$ we have $0<y<1.$\n\n![](images/16/16f3dc78752c8cfcb6b6968e3d57bb3639a4205e2a32dfd569c8c2ca3c29a589.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $0<y<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(\\frac{1}{X}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(X\\ge \\frac{1}{y}) \\\\  & =1-{F}_{X}(\\frac{1}{y})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $0<y<1,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0-(-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}})\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(\\frac{1}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{1}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{1}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{(\\frac{1}{y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ea541e01-5fa9-5c1a-9bd5-70920b6a9e22"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ea541e01-5fa9-5c1a-9bd5-70920b6a9e22" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea541e01-5fa9-5c1a-9bd5-70920b6a9e22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-53f11dd5-3815-523d-8b4f-218a0c887321" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7a5a5e16-2b43-5e40-8cb3-9fe6c9bc2a8c" "answer-53f11dd5-3815-523d-8b4f-218a0c887321" "answer-ee37ca3b-30b3-5807-a624-f62ac29989e2" "answer-e933345b-51e3-5f41-b177-21de967b42a8" "answer-76d37b1f-0cae-52e4-bbc9-ab6fd6b7061a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a5a5e16-2b43-5e40-8cb3-9fe6c9bc2a8c" :answer/id #uuid "7a5a5e16-2b43-5e40-8cb3-9fe6c9bc2a8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & -1<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53f11dd5-3815-523d-8b4f-218a0c887321" :answer/id #uuid "53f11dd5-3815-523d-8b4f-218a0c887321" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ee37ca3b-30b3-5807-a624-f62ac29989e2" :answer/id #uuid "ee37ca3b-30b3-5807-a624-f62ac29989e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x,\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e933345b-51e3-5f41-b177-21de967b42a8" :answer/id #uuid "e933345b-51e3-5f41-b177-21de967b42a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-y},\\, & y>0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76d37b1f-0cae-52e4-bbc9-ab6fd6b7061a" :answer/id #uuid "76d37b1f-0cae-52e4-bbc9-ab6fd6b7061a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y},\\, & y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1f799a56-7472-58ef-998d-84e22fb88853" :question/id #uuid "1f799a56-7472-58ef-998d-84e22fb88853" :question/math-academy-id "q-110126" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{4},\\, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=1-{X}^{5},$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=1-{X}^{5}$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $0<x<1,$ we have $0<y<1.$\n\n![](images/05/05534475aecc1d0ebad2234f1259d1b6fd1c6183e47ad763f17c87c5fdb06afb.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $0<y<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(1-{X}^{5}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(-{X}^{5}\\le y-1) \\\\  & =P(X\\ge (1-y)^{1/5}) \\\\  & =1-{F}_{X}((1-y)^{1/5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $0<y<1,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0-(-\\frac{1}{5(1-y)^{4/5}})\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}((1-y)^{1/5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5(1-y)^{4/5}}\\cdot {f}_{X}((1-y)^{1/5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{5(1-y)^{4/5}}\\cdot {f}_{X}((1-y)^{1/5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5(1-y)^{4/5}}\\cdot 5{((1-y)^{1/5})}^{4} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8bffd42c-4c16-5c26-a4d3-ff06e8bcf1b7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8bffd42c-4c16-5c26-a4d3-ff06e8bcf1b7" :answer-field/id #uuid "8bffd42c-4c16-5c26-a4d3-ff06e8bcf1b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-196dbf90-694f-56e1-bd9a-bacffff31ed3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d7e7845f-1c6b-5825-bbe7-1626dc1077e1" "answer-52cef4e5-3e19-5e35-bee0-384a657d1c16" "answer-196dbf90-694f-56e1-bd9a-bacffff31ed3" "answer-a623ad96-993c-5f91-994d-d43006007fb2" "answer-4ca12552-8ad4-5d6a-8884-8f4afde5830a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7e7845f-1c6b-5825-bbe7-1626dc1077e1" :answer/id #uuid "d7e7845f-1c6b-5825-bbe7-1626dc1077e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.5,\\, & 0<y<2 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52cef4e5-3e19-5e35-bee0-384a657d1c16" :answer/id #uuid "52cef4e5-3e19-5e35-bee0-384a657d1c16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.5y,\\, & 0<y<2 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-196dbf90-694f-56e1-bd9a-bacffff31ed3" :answer/id #uuid "196dbf90-694f-56e1-bd9a-bacffff31ed3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a623ad96-993c-5f91-994d-d43006007fb2" :answer/id #uuid "a623ad96-993c-5f91-994d-d43006007fb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2y,\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ca12552-8ad4-5d6a-8884-8f4afde5830a" :answer/id #uuid "4ca12552-8ad4-5d6a-8884-8f4afde5830a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}5,\\, & 0<y<0.2 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a4b19843-0372-523c-be3f-e38cf328fccc" :question/id #uuid "a4b19843-0372-523c-be3f-e38cf328fccc" :question/math-academy-id "q-110245" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that since the values of $X$ are $0<x<1,$ $Y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡X$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $0<x<1,$ we have $y>0.$\n\n![](images/5a/5a2a6f4c5e26819af509e9347fb7aff230927bdd9192ad10a48ce9c951c7be80.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $y>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡X\\le y) \\\\  & =P(\\operatorname{ln}⁡X\\ge -y) \\\\  & =P(X\\ge {e}^{-y}) \\\\  & =1-{F}_{X}({e}^{-y})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $y>0,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0-(-{e}^{-y})\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}({e}^{-y}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-y}\\cdot {f}_{X}({e}^{-y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={e}^{-y}\\cdot {f}_{X}({e}^{-y}) \\\\  & ={e}^{-y}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={e}^{-y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-y}\\, & y>0 \\\\ 0\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f2a17ede-9d12-55e8-9a15-7ee9a3ba31af"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f2a17ede-9d12-55e8-9a15-7ee9a3ba31af" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a17ede-9d12-55e8-9a15-7ee9a3ba31af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-98739189-0bce-58a6-b3ce-c59b0a5d2aad" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3137f17a-3a0e-5b0c-a694-056680cb7764" "answer-02cf00d4-bb82-5dd8-a677-72fc28f792e6" "answer-59577974-15fa-52fa-8f57-a46673040992" "answer-98739189-0bce-58a6-b3ce-c59b0a5d2aad" "answer-7105b7b3-58d8-53b8-a82e-927f96c5336f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3137f17a-3a0e-5b0c-a694-056680cb7764" :answer/id #uuid "3137f17a-3a0e-5b0c-a694-056680cb7764" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02cf00d4-bb82-5dd8-a677-72fc28f792e6" :answer/id #uuid "02cf00d4-bb82-5dd8-a677-72fc28f792e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2y}\\, & y>0 \\\\ 0\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59577974-15fa-52fa-8f57-a46673040992" :answer/id #uuid "59577974-15fa-52fa-8f57-a46673040992" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2y}\\, & y<0 \\\\ 0\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-98739189-0bce-58a6-b3ce-c59b0a5d2aad" :answer/id #uuid "98739189-0bce-58a6-b3ce-c59b0a5d2aad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-y}\\, & y>0 \\\\ 0\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7105b7b3-58d8-53b8-a82e-927f96c5336f" :answer/id #uuid "7105b7b3-58d8-53b8-a82e-927f96c5336f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{y}\\, & y<0 \\\\ 0\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-75b7b0a4-c7ee-525c-b9ca-1a7df7652ed9" :question/id #uuid "75b7b0a4-c7ee-525c-b9ca-1a7df7652ed9" :question/math-academy-id "q-110343" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{-4x},\\, & x>0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=-\\sqrt[3]{X},$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=-\\sqrt[3]{X}$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $x>0,$ we have $y<0.$\n\n![](images/4c/4c2b1503e6624c9060829468c9fa0d49856a2d76131975b6b1e437b7de3285c7.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $y<0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(-\\sqrt[3]{X}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(-X\\le {y}^{3}) \\\\  & =P(X\\ge -{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =1-{F}_{X}(-{y}^{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $y>0,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0-(-3{y}^{2})\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(-{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(-{y}^{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =3{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(-{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}\\cdot 4{e}^{-4(-{y}^{3})} \\\\  & =12{y}^{2}{e}^{4{y}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}12{y}^{2}{e}^{4{y}^{3}},\\, & y<0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-98d1d0c4-c915-5b43-86d2-eae585442104"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-98d1d0c4-c915-5b43-86d2-eae585442104" :answer-field/id #uuid "98d1d0c4-c915-5b43-86d2-eae585442104" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ce9720cc-9e97-5b98-9dc1-bae43a45708b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f63e4602-5159-57f7-952a-0152cc8abc16" "answer-8f4a131d-65cf-5e71-9eb3-dac170dbbf51" "answer-acfa5a4c-add0-565a-9ded-15a152272ac5" "answer-ce9720cc-9e97-5b98-9dc1-bae43a45708b" "answer-679eafa7-4671-5f81-9026-857bfb15b568"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f63e4602-5159-57f7-952a-0152cc8abc16" :answer/id #uuid "f63e4602-5159-57f7-952a-0152cc8abc16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}12{e}^{-12y},\\, & y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f4a131d-65cf-5e71-9eb3-dac170dbbf51" :answer/id #uuid "8f4a131d-65cf-5e71-9eb3-dac170dbbf51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}12{e}^{12y},\\, & y<0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-acfa5a4c-add0-565a-9ded-15a152272ac5" :answer/id #uuid "acfa5a4c-add0-565a-9ded-15a152272ac5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}12{y}^{2}{e}^{-4{y}^{3}},\\, & y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce9720cc-9e97-5b98-9dc1-bae43a45708b" :answer/id #uuid "ce9720cc-9e97-5b98-9dc1-bae43a45708b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}12{y}^{2}{e}^{4{y}^{3}},\\, & y<0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-679eafa7-4671-5f81-9026-857bfb15b568" :answer/id #uuid "679eafa7-4671-5f81-9026-857bfb15b568" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{4y},\\, & y<0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163263 :tutorial/content "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable whose probability density function is known. Suppose we want to define a new random variable $Y$ as\n\n$$\nY = u(X),\n$$\n\nwhere $u = u(X)$ is a function of $X.$ How do we find the probability density function of $Y?$\n\nTo find the PDF of $Y,$ we can use the **distribution function method**. The distribution function method consists of two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for $F_Y$ in terms of $F_X,$ where $F_Y$ and $F_X$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate $F_Y$ to get the probability density function $f_Y$ of $Y.$\n\nIn this lesson, we'll assume that the function $u$ is strictly monotonic (i.e., strictly increasing or decreasing). The case where $u$ is not monotonic will be dealt with in a future lesson.\n\nLet's see an example of the distribution function method in action." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163339 :tutorial/content "Suppose the continuous random variable $X$ is defined as\n\n![](images/88/88103878042469595fc8f8243958b44b128c0d38465bfe93a31f83afd6988300.svg)\nLet $Y= 1+2X.$ Let's use the distribution function method to find the probability density function of $Y.$\n\nFirst, note that $Y = 1+2X$ is a strictly increasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $x > 0,$ we have $y > 1.$\n\n![](images/54/544e551755f4c8a575ef227b77fe520deec203f08654eec31109e496141aa91c.png)\n\nLet's consider $y > 1.$ We write down the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ and then use our transformation to isolate $X$ in the parentheses. This will allow us to write $F_Y$ in terms of $F_X\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(2X+1\\le y) \\\\  & =P(2X\\le y-1) \\\\  & =P(X\\le \\frac{y-1}{2}) \\\\  & ={F}_{X}(\\frac{y-1}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the PDF $f_Y(y)$ for $y > 1,$ we differentiate $F_Y$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({F}_{X}(\\frac{y-1}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{y-1}{2})\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(\\frac{y-1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(\\frac{y-1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{y-1}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of $f_X,$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{y-1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {e}^{-(y-1)/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{(1-y)/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{(1-y)/2}, & \\,y>1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt's easy (and often worthwhile) to check that this is a valid probability density function." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162191 :activity/expected-seconds 840.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186161846 :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n![](images/50/501074b2c8aa951c9236dc628de2a564f31b21b5ac5b4dd34d7b1324d4c8a331.svg)\nIf $Y =1-3X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$"] [17592186161846 :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y = u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for $F_Y$ terms of $F_X,$ where $F_Y$ and $F_X$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate $F_Y$ to get the probability density function $f_Y.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y = 1-3X$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X.$  Moreover, for $0 < x < 1,$ we have $-2 \\lt y \\lt 1 .$\n\n![](images/3b/3bb641b1920d0ded33e4ffa25f3e0af856550dd3820edf30416bd79c3a6da264.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $-2 \\lt y \\lt 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(1-3X\\le y) \\\\  & =P(-3X\\le y-1) \\\\  & =P(X\\ge \\frac{1-y}{3}) \\\\  & =1-{F}_{X}(\\frac{1-y}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF $f_Y(y)$ for $-2 \\lt y \\lt 1,$ we differentiate $F_Y$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0-(-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(\\frac{1-y}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{1-y}{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of $f_X,$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{1-y}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 2\\cdot (\\frac{1-y}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(1-y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n![](images/b0/b00d02901c82c0544e8e576577832184919da2338cf05d2d8a3fa230d45993c4.svg)"] [17592186161847 :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n![](images/33/3357fbadc12363114c7274b17df9f8e992566d53f8233841783338687b88989e.svg)\nIf $Y = (2-X)^3,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$"] [17592186161847 :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y = u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for $F_Y$ terms of $F_X,$ where $F_Y$ and $F_X$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate $F_Y$ to get the probability density function $f_Y.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y = (2-X)^3$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $0 \\lt x \\lt 2,$ we have $0 \\lt y \\lt 8 .$\n\n![](images/2c/2c07ffe5af282ba1689cb6f49201b979afb4186d0128dd6a97f446b7240d76d6.png)\n\n \n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $0 \\lt y \\lt 8,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P((2-X)^{3}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(2-X\\le {y}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =P(-X\\le {y}^{1/3}-2) \\\\  & =P(X\\ge 2-{y}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =1-{F}_{X}(2-{y}^{1/3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF $f_Y(y)$ for $0 \\lt y \\lt 8,$ we differentiate $F_Y$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0-(-\\frac{1}{3{y}^{2/3}})\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(2-{y}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{y}^{2/3}}\\cdot {f}_{X}(2-{y}^{1/3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of $f_X,$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{3{y}^{2/3}}\\cdot {f}_{X}(2-{y}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{y}^{2/3}}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}(2-(2-{y}^{1/3}))^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{y}^{2/3}}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}(2-2+{y}^{1/3})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3{y}^{2/3}}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}({y}^{1/3})^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n![](images/d8/d858994c802b37d5867c0b8940848fec484bf42c48ecb525c5d518165ade60c6.svg)"] [17592186162248 :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{-4x},\\, & x>0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=2X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$"] [17592186162248 :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=2X$ is a strictly increasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $x>0,$ we have $y>0.$\n\n![](images/8b/8b2d1487d180db1df306cd8c83088ef0334d29769bd7ef94eed7f75d4e6cedf7.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $y>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(2X\\le y) \\\\  & =P(X\\le \\frac{y}{2}) \\\\  & ={F}_{X}(\\frac{y}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $y>0,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(\\frac{y}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{y}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{y}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4{e}^{-4\\cdot y/2} \\\\  & =2{e}^{-2y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2y}, & \\,y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186162248 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-69593d18-dc90-550d-8f2b-fef2e3f9c883" :answer/id #uuid "69593d18-dc90-550d-8f2b-fef2e3f9c883"] ["answer-69593d18-dc90-550d-8f2b-fef2e3f9c883" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-69593d18-dc90-550d-8f2b-fef2e3f9c883" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2y}, & \\,y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-600d0ed3-d6f7-5bed-9243-c5cd652cb251" :answer/id #uuid "600d0ed3-d6f7-5bed-9243-c5cd652cb251"] ["answer-600d0ed3-d6f7-5bed-9243-c5cd652cb251" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-600d0ed3-d6f7-5bed-9243-c5cd652cb251" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-4y}, & \\,y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-bf7be294-62d9-5518-9eb0-0262367daae6" :answer/id #uuid "bf7be294-62d9-5518-9eb0-0262367daae6"] ["answer-bf7be294-62d9-5518-9eb0-0262367daae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bf7be294-62d9-5518-9eb0-0262367daae6" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}8{e}^{-8y}, & \\,y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-39e8db46-65a2-5088-a0fc-7d008a801433" :answer/id #uuid "39e8db46-65a2-5088-a0fc-7d008a801433"] ["answer-39e8db46-65a2-5088-a0fc-7d008a801433" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-39e8db46-65a2-5088-a0fc-7d008a801433" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-4y}, & \\,y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-0d7fa984-dcc6-51d3-a178-09d0e7e701a1" :answer/id #uuid "0d7fa984-dcc6-51d3-a178-09d0e7e701a1"] ["answer-0d7fa984-dcc6-51d3-a178-09d0e7e701a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0d7fa984-dcc6-51d3-a178-09d0e7e701a1" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{-4y}, & \\,y>0 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] [17592186158690 :answer-field/correct "answer-69593d18-dc90-550d-8f2b-fef2e3f9c883"] [17592186158690 :answer-field/choices "answer-69593d18-dc90-550d-8f2b-fef2e3f9c883"] [17592186158690 :answer-field/choices "answer-600d0ed3-d6f7-5bed-9243-c5cd652cb251"] [17592186158690 :answer-field/choices "answer-bf7be294-62d9-5518-9eb0-0262367daae6"] [17592186158690 :answer-field/choices "answer-39e8db46-65a2-5088-a0fc-7d008a801433"] [17592186158690 :answer-field/choices "answer-0d7fa984-dcc6-51d3-a178-09d0e7e701a1"] ["question-7be864d2-62c5-5172-87fe-bf187923ab8c" :question/id #uuid "7be864d2-62c5-5172-87fe-bf187923ab8c"] ["question-7be864d2-62c5-5172-87fe-bf187923ab8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-151981"] ["question-7be864d2-62c5-5172-87fe-bf187923ab8c" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}(1-{x}^{2}),\\, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=\\frac{X}{3},$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$"] ["question-7be864d2-62c5-5172-87fe-bf187923ab8c" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ in terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=\\frac{X}{3}$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $0<x<1,$ we have $0<y<\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\n![](images/42/42a3c2510927b66842ec0360eabfb169a306ccaf52292132f31769036e608e69.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $0<y<\\frac{1}{3},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(\\frac{X}{3}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 3y) \\\\  & ={F}_{X}(3y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $0<y<\\frac{1}{3},$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(3y) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {f}_{X}(3y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =3\\cdot {f}_{X}(3y) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(1-(3y)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}(1-9{y}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{2}(1-9{y}^{2}), & \\,0<y<\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-7be864d2-62c5-5172-87fe-bf187923ab8c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-85d2285e-2456-56af-a314-257530350a9e" :answer-field/id #uuid "85d2285e-2456-56af-a314-257530350a9e"] ["answer-b55a125e-dbc5-56ad-bd31-db73ae35ac74" :answer/id #uuid "b55a125e-dbc5-56ad-bd31-db73ae35ac74"] ["answer-b55a125e-dbc5-56ad-bd31-db73ae35ac74" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b55a125e-dbc5-56ad-bd31-db73ae35ac74" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{18}(9-{y}^{2}), & \\,0<y<3 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-2d7990c6-c565-5878-9b66-56ed047222ca" :answer/id #uuid "2d7990c6-c565-5878-9b66-56ed047222ca"] ["answer-2d7990c6-c565-5878-9b66-56ed047222ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2d7990c6-c565-5878-9b66-56ed047222ca" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}(1-9{y}^{2}), & \\,0<y<\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-202d7c13-d634-5a77-af5c-845389655864" :answer/id #uuid "202d7c13-d634-5a77-af5c-845389655864"] ["answer-202d7c13-d634-5a77-af5c-845389655864" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-202d7c13-d634-5a77-af5c-845389655864" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}(9-{y}^{2}), & \\,0<y<3 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-a839825b-9be8-5988-b3e5-e0aa662c915b" :answer/id #uuid "a839825b-9be8-5988-b3e5-e0aa662c915b"] ["answer-a839825b-9be8-5988-b3e5-e0aa662c915b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a839825b-9be8-5988-b3e5-e0aa662c915b" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{27}{8}(1-3{y}^{2}), & \\,0<y<\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-09920ab5-927e-5144-b904-cafb0b14ca5b" :answer/id #uuid "09920ab5-927e-5144-b904-cafb0b14ca5b"] ["answer-09920ab5-927e-5144-b904-cafb0b14ca5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-09920ab5-927e-5144-b904-cafb0b14ca5b" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{2}(1-9{y}^{2}), & \\,0<y<\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-field-85d2285e-2456-56af-a314-257530350a9e" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-85d2285e-2456-56af-a314-257530350a9e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-85d2285e-2456-56af-a314-257530350a9e" :answer-field/correct "answer-09920ab5-927e-5144-b904-cafb0b14ca5b"] ["answer-field-85d2285e-2456-56af-a314-257530350a9e" :answer-field/choices "answer-b55a125e-dbc5-56ad-bd31-db73ae35ac74"] ["answer-field-85d2285e-2456-56af-a314-257530350a9e" :answer-field/choices "answer-2d7990c6-c565-5878-9b66-56ed047222ca"] ["answer-field-85d2285e-2456-56af-a314-257530350a9e" :answer-field/choices "answer-202d7c13-d634-5a77-af5c-845389655864"] ["answer-field-85d2285e-2456-56af-a314-257530350a9e" :answer-field/choices "answer-a839825b-9be8-5988-b3e5-e0aa662c915b"] ["answer-field-85d2285e-2456-56af-a314-257530350a9e" :answer-field/choices "answer-09920ab5-927e-5144-b904-cafb0b14ca5b"] ["question-7be864d2-62c5-5172-87fe-bf187923ab8c" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-85d2285e-2456-56af-a314-257530350a9e"] [17592186162046 :knowledge-point/questions "question-7be864d2-62c5-5172-87fe-bf187923ab8c"] ["question-09cc9808-be42-54c9-b4a2-69b0d9a20cf1" :question/id #uuid "09cc9808-be42-54c9-b4a2-69b0d9a20cf1"] ["question-09cc9808-be42-54c9-b4a2-69b0d9a20cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-110111"] ["question-09cc9808-be42-54c9-b4a2-69b0d9a20cf1" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x,\\, & -1<x<0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=10X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$"] ["question-09cc9808-be42-54c9-b4a2-69b0d9a20cf1" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=10X$ is a strictly increasing function of $X.$ Moreover, for $-1<x<0,$ we have $-10<y<0.$\n\n![](images/4b/4b03f4d44db5b0db0498469f80fa25e56177a8602c657d8506105837212bf5ba.png)\n\n*Note: Image not drawn to scale.*\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $-10<y<0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(10X\\le y) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 0.1y) \\\\  & ={F}_{X}(0.1y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $-10<y<0,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0.1\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(0.1y) \\\\  & =0.1\\cdot {f}_{X}(0.1y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =0.1\\cdot {f}_{X}(0.1y) \\\\  & =0.1\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 0.1y \\\\  & =-0.02y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-0.02y, & -10<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-09cc9808-be42-54c9-b4a2-69b0d9a20cf1" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-a19812d1-1d0a-5303-9a54-a3aaf278c49f" :answer-field/id #uuid "a19812d1-1d0a-5303-9a54-a3aaf278c49f"] ["answer-f894221d-2427-5570-8811-51ea50f7082e" :answer/id #uuid "f894221d-2427-5570-8811-51ea50f7082e"] ["answer-f894221d-2427-5570-8811-51ea50f7082e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f894221d-2427-5570-8811-51ea50f7082e" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-0.02y, & -10<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-580d8eab-cee9-52ff-8594-cc7c4cf9f774" :answer/id #uuid "580d8eab-cee9-52ff-8594-cc7c4cf9f774"] ["answer-580d8eab-cee9-52ff-8594-cc7c4cf9f774" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-580d8eab-cee9-52ff-8594-cc7c4cf9f774" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-200y, & -0.1<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-f445b8e1-6995-53c8-b3fe-7a9a2f3140f8" :answer/id #uuid "f445b8e1-6995-53c8-b3fe-7a9a2f3140f8"] ["answer-f445b8e1-6995-53c8-b3fe-7a9a2f3140f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f445b8e1-6995-53c8-b3fe-7a9a2f3140f8" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.002{y}^{2}, & -10<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-533ff78c-a4d2-572e-aa52-f826f311b683" :answer/id #uuid "533ff78c-a4d2-572e-aa52-f826f311b683"] ["answer-533ff78c-a4d2-572e-aa52-f826f311b683" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-533ff78c-a4d2-572e-aa52-f826f311b683" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.02y, & 0<y<10 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-ed5095e2-f6a2-5b2f-833a-1ffb143c4f3f" :answer/id #uuid "ed5095e2-f6a2-5b2f-833a-1ffb143c4f3f"] ["answer-ed5095e2-f6a2-5b2f-833a-1ffb143c4f3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ed5095e2-f6a2-5b2f-833a-1ffb143c4f3f" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2y, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-field-a19812d1-1d0a-5303-9a54-a3aaf278c49f" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-a19812d1-1d0a-5303-9a54-a3aaf278c49f" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-a19812d1-1d0a-5303-9a54-a3aaf278c49f" :answer-field/correct "answer-f894221d-2427-5570-8811-51ea50f7082e"] ["answer-field-a19812d1-1d0a-5303-9a54-a3aaf278c49f" :answer-field/choices "answer-f894221d-2427-5570-8811-51ea50f7082e"] ["answer-field-a19812d1-1d0a-5303-9a54-a3aaf278c49f" :answer-field/choices "answer-580d8eab-cee9-52ff-8594-cc7c4cf9f774"] ["answer-field-a19812d1-1d0a-5303-9a54-a3aaf278c49f" :answer-field/choices "answer-f445b8e1-6995-53c8-b3fe-7a9a2f3140f8"] ["answer-field-a19812d1-1d0a-5303-9a54-a3aaf278c49f" :answer-field/choices "answer-533ff78c-a4d2-572e-aa52-f826f311b683"] ["answer-field-a19812d1-1d0a-5303-9a54-a3aaf278c49f" :answer-field/choices "answer-ed5095e2-f6a2-5b2f-833a-1ffb143c4f3f"] ["question-09cc9808-be42-54c9-b4a2-69b0d9a20cf1" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-a19812d1-1d0a-5303-9a54-a3aaf278c49f"] [17592186162046 :knowledge-point/questions "question-09cc9808-be42-54c9-b4a2-69b0d9a20cf1"] ["question-8460a557-83b6-5efd-a8a5-c94e63881b6d" :question/id #uuid "8460a557-83b6-5efd-a8a5-c94e63881b6d"] ["question-8460a557-83b6-5efd-a8a5-c94e63881b6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-151985"] ["question-8460a557-83b6-5efd-a8a5-c94e63881b6d" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{3},\\, & 1<x<2 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=2X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$"] ["question-8460a557-83b6-5efd-a8a5-c94e63881b6d" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ in terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=2X$ is a strictly increasing function of $X.$  Moreover, for $1<x<2,$ we have $2<y<4.$\n\n![](images/60/60342277a025cb26cebab2ac534fad4aa1b49fc2285571c303c4e829eb464606.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $2<y<4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(2X\\le y) \\\\  & =P(X\\le \\frac{y}{2}) \\\\  & ={F}_{X}(\\frac{y}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $2<y<4,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(\\frac{y}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{y}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{y}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2(\\frac{y}{2})}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{6}, & \\,2<y<4 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-8460a557-83b6-5efd-a8a5-c94e63881b6d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-69f2e9ff-fa41-50ab-a63c-2d1d1f490067" :answer-field/id #uuid "69f2e9ff-fa41-50ab-a63c-2d1d1f490067"] ["answer-165a73fa-f469-5a44-86ef-009948eb5611" :answer/id #uuid "165a73fa-f469-5a44-86ef-009948eb5611"] ["answer-165a73fa-f469-5a44-86ef-009948eb5611" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-165a73fa-f469-5a44-86ef-009948eb5611" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}, & \\,1<y<2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-0b7bf6b1-d530-59ea-9dc8-7b99db3d0094" :answer/id #uuid "0b7bf6b1-d530-59ea-9dc8-7b99db3d0094"] ["answer-0b7bf6b1-d530-59ea-9dc8-7b99db3d0094" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0b7bf6b1-d530-59ea-9dc8-7b99db3d0094" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4y}{3}, & \\,2<y<4 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-d167a7a8-34d5-59c3-b949-f001717e3bd9" :answer/id #uuid "d167a7a8-34d5-59c3-b949-f001717e3bd9"] ["answer-d167a7a8-34d5-59c3-b949-f001717e3bd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d167a7a8-34d5-59c3-b949-f001717e3bd9" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{3}, & \\,2<y<4 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-1fc1534a-6a01-51a4-9c6e-4184dd7e0bcc" :answer/id #uuid "1fc1534a-6a01-51a4-9c6e-4184dd7e0bcc"] ["answer-1fc1534a-6a01-51a4-9c6e-4184dd7e0bcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1fc1534a-6a01-51a4-9c6e-4184dd7e0bcc" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{6}, & \\,1<y<2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-b5dc456d-f743-5286-851a-c035feeffac9" :answer/id #uuid "b5dc456d-f743-5286-851a-c035feeffac9"] ["answer-b5dc456d-f743-5286-851a-c035feeffac9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b5dc456d-f743-5286-851a-c035feeffac9" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{6}, & \\,2<y<4 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-field-69f2e9ff-fa41-50ab-a63c-2d1d1f490067" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-69f2e9ff-fa41-50ab-a63c-2d1d1f490067" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-69f2e9ff-fa41-50ab-a63c-2d1d1f490067" :answer-field/correct "answer-b5dc456d-f743-5286-851a-c035feeffac9"] ["answer-field-69f2e9ff-fa41-50ab-a63c-2d1d1f490067" :answer-field/choices "answer-165a73fa-f469-5a44-86ef-009948eb5611"] ["answer-field-69f2e9ff-fa41-50ab-a63c-2d1d1f490067" :answer-field/choices "answer-0b7bf6b1-d530-59ea-9dc8-7b99db3d0094"] ["answer-field-69f2e9ff-fa41-50ab-a63c-2d1d1f490067" :answer-field/choices "answer-d167a7a8-34d5-59c3-b949-f001717e3bd9"] ["answer-field-69f2e9ff-fa41-50ab-a63c-2d1d1f490067" :answer-field/choices "answer-1fc1534a-6a01-51a4-9c6e-4184dd7e0bcc"] ["answer-field-69f2e9ff-fa41-50ab-a63c-2d1d1f490067" :answer-field/choices "answer-b5dc456d-f743-5286-851a-c035feeffac9"] ["question-8460a557-83b6-5efd-a8a5-c94e63881b6d" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-69f2e9ff-fa41-50ab-a63c-2d1d1f490067"] [17592186162046 :knowledge-point/questions "question-8460a557-83b6-5efd-a8a5-c94e63881b6d"] ["question-37fc4f1c-699a-5034-b164-6cf41c6e46b4" :question/id #uuid "37fc4f1c-699a-5034-b164-6cf41c6e46b4"] ["question-37fc4f1c-699a-5034-b164-6cf41c6e46b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-110106"] ["question-37fc4f1c-699a-5034-b164-6cf41c6e46b4" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2},\\, & 0<x<3 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=1-\\frac{1}{3}X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$"] ["question-37fc4f1c-699a-5034-b164-6cf41c6e46b4" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that $Y=1-\\frac{1}{3}X$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X.$  Moreover, for $0<x<3,$ we have $0<y<1.$\n\n![](images/af/afe10720ce51bc3dd1b304ea276568d0e505f90159359f5ae54462e4caa729e7.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $0<y<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(1-\\frac{X}{3}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(-X\\le 3y-3) \\\\  & =P(X\\ge 3-3y) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 3-3y) \\\\  & =1-{F}_{X}(3-3y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $0<y<1,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0-(-3)\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(3-3y) \\\\  & =3\\cdot {f}_{X}(3-3y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =3\\cdot {f}_{X}(3-3y) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}(3-3y)^{2} \\\\  & =3{(1-y)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{(1-y)}^{2},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-37fc4f1c-699a-5034-b164-6cf41c6e46b4" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-5108732e-f4b1-55bf-ab3d-9aaa670d4ed1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5108732e-f4b1-55bf-ab3d-9aaa670d4ed1"] ["answer-472e5251-de8e-5c8f-906b-4486590c0f4f" :answer/id #uuid "472e5251-de8e-5c8f-906b-4486590c0f4f"] ["answer-472e5251-de8e-5c8f-906b-4486590c0f4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-472e5251-de8e-5c8f-906b-4486590c0f4f" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2(1-y),\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-46564b22-49a3-5dd7-851e-0ef24aa530e9" :answer/id #uuid "46564b22-49a3-5dd7-851e-0ef24aa530e9"] ["answer-46564b22-49a3-5dd7-851e-0ef24aa530e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-46564b22-49a3-5dd7-851e-0ef24aa530e9" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{(1+y)}^{2},\\, & -1<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-8a45c7a0-ff71-52fb-9d02-51c4c15a7b53" :answer/id #uuid "8a45c7a0-ff71-52fb-9d02-51c4c15a7b53"] ["answer-8a45c7a0-ff71-52fb-9d02-51c4c15a7b53" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8a45c7a0-ff71-52fb-9d02-51c4c15a7b53" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{(1-y)}^{2},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-6f344b2d-2e68-5f7d-a74f-c89cb5cf5253" :answer/id #uuid "6f344b2d-2e68-5f7d-a74f-c89cb5cf5253"] ["answer-6f344b2d-2e68-5f7d-a74f-c89cb5cf5253" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6f344b2d-2e68-5f7d-a74f-c89cb5cf5253" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2},\\, & -1<y<0 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-53f81be5-441e-51b6-84d8-52f835d28bfb" :answer/id #uuid "53f81be5-441e-51b6-84d8-52f835d28bfb"] ["answer-53f81be5-441e-51b6-84d8-52f835d28bfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-53f81be5-441e-51b6-84d8-52f835d28bfb" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-field-5108732e-f4b1-55bf-ab3d-9aaa670d4ed1" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-5108732e-f4b1-55bf-ab3d-9aaa670d4ed1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-5108732e-f4b1-55bf-ab3d-9aaa670d4ed1" :answer-field/correct "answer-8a45c7a0-ff71-52fb-9d02-51c4c15a7b53"] ["answer-field-5108732e-f4b1-55bf-ab3d-9aaa670d4ed1" :answer-field/choices "answer-472e5251-de8e-5c8f-906b-4486590c0f4f"] ["answer-field-5108732e-f4b1-55bf-ab3d-9aaa670d4ed1" :answer-field/choices "answer-46564b22-49a3-5dd7-851e-0ef24aa530e9"] ["answer-field-5108732e-f4b1-55bf-ab3d-9aaa670d4ed1" :answer-field/choices "answer-8a45c7a0-ff71-52fb-9d02-51c4c15a7b53"] ["answer-field-5108732e-f4b1-55bf-ab3d-9aaa670d4ed1" :answer-field/choices "answer-6f344b2d-2e68-5f7d-a74f-c89cb5cf5253"] ["answer-field-5108732e-f4b1-55bf-ab3d-9aaa670d4ed1" :answer-field/choices "answer-53f81be5-441e-51b6-84d8-52f835d28bfb"] ["question-37fc4f1c-699a-5034-b164-6cf41c6e46b4" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-5108732e-f4b1-55bf-ab3d-9aaa670d4ed1"] [17592186162046 :knowledge-point/questions "question-37fc4f1c-699a-5034-b164-6cf41c6e46b4"] ["question-670a140c-55d4-5114-b612-9d3a283512c3" :question/id #uuid "670a140c-55d4-5114-b612-9d3a283512c3"] ["question-670a140c-55d4-5114-b612-9d3a283512c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-110124"] ["question-670a140c-55d4-5114-b612-9d3a283512c3" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x,\\, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y={X}^{4},$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$"] ["question-670a140c-55d4-5114-b612-9d3a283512c3" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note  that since the possible values of $X$ are $0<x<1,$ $Y={X}^{4}$ is a strictly increasing function of $X$ when $0<x<1.$ Moreover, for $0<x<1,$ we have $0<y<1.$\n\n![](images/9a/9a6f01a3538711e45e581038af5eaf95e229bf72d08bafefbcf34786a40c1d2d.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $0<y<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P({X}^{4}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(X\\le {y}^{1/4}) \\\\  & ={F}_{X}({y}^{1/4})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $0<y<1,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{y}^{3/4}}\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}({y}^{1/4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{y}^{3/4}}\\cdot {f}_{X}({y}^{1/4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{4{y}^{3/4}}\\cdot {f}_{X}({y}^{1/4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4{y}^{3/4}}\\cdot 2({y}^{1/4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-670a140c-55d4-5114-b612-9d3a283512c3" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-38e37aa3-43fc-561c-9a91-d1b0e6848656" :answer-field/id #uuid "38e37aa3-43fc-561c-9a91-d1b0e6848656"] ["answer-513b7cbf-3854-54d3-8df7-b61ae060993c" :answer/id #uuid "513b7cbf-3854-54d3-8df7-b61ae060993c"] ["answer-513b7cbf-3854-54d3-8df7-b61ae060993c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-513b7cbf-3854-54d3-8df7-b61ae060993c" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-ee1549c6-a005-585d-aaa9-47cb105e6439" :answer/id #uuid "ee1549c6-a005-585d-aaa9-47cb105e6439"] ["answer-ee1549c6-a005-585d-aaa9-47cb105e6439" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ee1549c6-a005-585d-aaa9-47cb105e6439" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-e1de8cd4-39ab-557a-bd23-6dbdab09b64c" :answer/id #uuid "e1de8cd4-39ab-557a-bd23-6dbdab09b64c"] ["answer-e1de8cd4-39ab-557a-bd23-6dbdab09b64c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e1de8cd4-39ab-557a-bd23-6dbdab09b64c" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{y},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-100bdc8b-84b9-522b-95a8-62a7c19d7ac1" :answer/id #uuid "100bdc8b-84b9-522b-95a8-62a7c19d7ac1"] ["answer-100bdc8b-84b9-522b-95a8-62a7c19d7ac1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-100bdc8b-84b9-522b-95a8-62a7c19d7ac1" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4\\sqrt[4]{y}},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-1da9150a-4f27-53df-84d6-afffbc13c04b" :answer/id #uuid "1da9150a-4f27-53df-84d6-afffbc13c04b"] ["answer-1da9150a-4f27-53df-84d6-afffbc13c04b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1da9150a-4f27-53df-84d6-afffbc13c04b" :answer/value "{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt{{y}^{3}},\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}"] ["answer-field-38e37aa3-43fc-561c-9a91-d1b0e6848656" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-38e37aa3-43fc-561c-9a91-d1b0e6848656" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-38e37aa3-43fc-561c-9a91-d1b0e6848656" :answer-field/correct "answer-ee1549c6-a005-585d-aaa9-47cb105e6439"] ["answer-field-38e37aa3-43fc-561c-9a91-d1b0e6848656" :answer-field/choices "answer-513b7cbf-3854-54d3-8df7-b61ae060993c"] ["answer-field-38e37aa3-43fc-561c-9a91-d1b0e6848656" :answer-field/choices "answer-ee1549c6-a005-585d-aaa9-47cb105e6439"] ["answer-field-38e37aa3-43fc-561c-9a91-d1b0e6848656" :answer-field/choices "answer-e1de8cd4-39ab-557a-bd23-6dbdab09b64c"] ["answer-field-38e37aa3-43fc-561c-9a91-d1b0e6848656" :answer-field/choices "answer-100bdc8b-84b9-522b-95a8-62a7c19d7ac1"] ["answer-field-38e37aa3-43fc-561c-9a91-d1b0e6848656" :answer-field/choices "answer-1da9150a-4f27-53df-84d6-afffbc13c04b"] ["question-670a140c-55d4-5114-b612-9d3a283512c3" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-38e37aa3-43fc-561c-9a91-d1b0e6848656"] [17592186162047 :knowledge-point/questions "question-670a140c-55d4-5114-b612-9d3a283512c3"] ["question-f3a2a8f5-8f7b-5578-9df3-f4e28dce2d10" :question/id #uuid "f3a2a8f5-8f7b-5578-9df3-f4e28dce2d10"] ["question-f3a2a8f5-8f7b-5578-9df3-f4e28dce2d10" :question/math-academy-id "q-110130"] ["question-f3a2a8f5-8f7b-5578-9df3-f4e28dce2d10" :question/problem "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\, & x>1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=\\frac{1}{X},$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$"] ["question-f3a2a8f5-8f7b-5578-9df3-f4e28dce2d10" :question/worked-solution "To compute the probability density function of a random variable $Y,$ where $Y=u(X)$ is a continuous, strictly monotonic function of a continuous random variable $X,$ we follow two steps:\n\n- First, we find an expression for ${F}_{Y}$ terms of ${F}_{X},$ where ${F}_{Y}$ and ${F}_{X}$ are the cumulative distribution functions of $Y$ and $X,$ respectively.\n\n- Then, we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ to get the probability density function ${f}_{Y}.$\n\nBefore we start, note that the possible values of $X$ are $x\\in (1,\\infty ),$ and $Y=\\frac{1}{X}$ is a strictly decreasing function of $X$ when $X>1.$\n Moreover, for $x>1,$ we have $0<y<1.$\n\n![](images/16/16f3dc78752c8cfcb6b6968e3d57bb3639a4205e2a32dfd569c8c2ca3c29a589.png)\n\nNow, using the definition of the cumulative distribution of $Y,$ for $0<y<1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}_{Y}(y) & =P(Y\\le y) \\\\  & =P(\\frac{1}{X}\\le y) \\\\  & =P(X\\ge \\frac{1}{y}) \\\\  & =1-{F}_{X}(\\frac{1}{y})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the PDF ${f}_{Y}(y)$ for $0<y<1,$ we differentiate ${F}_{Y}$ with respect to $y$ using the chain rule. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={F}_{Y}^{′}(y) \\\\  & =0-(-\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}})\\cdot {F}_{X}^{′}(\\frac{1}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{1}{y}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of ${f}_{X},$ we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot {f}_{X}(\\frac{1}{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{(\\frac{1}{y})}^{2}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the PDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0<y<1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-f3a2a8f5-8f7b-5578-9df3-f4e28dce2d10" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-ea541e01-5fa9-5c1a-9bd5-70920b6a9e22" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea541e01-5fa9-5c1a-9bd5-70920b6a9e22"] ["answer-7a5a5e16-2b43-5e40-8cb3-9fe6c9bc2a8c" :answer/id #uuid "7a5a5e16-2b43-5e40-8cb3-9fe6c9bc2a8c"] ["answer-7a5a5e16-2b43-5e40-8cb3-9fe6c9bc2a8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7a5a5e16-2b43-5e40-8